1. What is committed here, and what it is not
---------------------------------------------

`verdicts/` holds our own measurements: for each released instance, which judge
was asked, under which framing, and what it answered. No question, document,
context passage or candidate answer from any source benchmark appears in it.

It is additionally a *projection* rather than the measurement in full: the judge's
generated text is dropped, because nothing here reads it, which is what takes the
tree from about 160 MB to about 5 MB. The complete verdicts, generations included,
ship in raim-verdicts (https://github.com/eOnofri04/raim-verdicts), committed
as runs.tar.xz. Nothing analytical is lost
— every table and figure in the paper regenerates from what is here, verified by
rebuilding all of them from this projection alone.

`derived/` holds what `make derive` computes from that: intervals, aggregation
ladders, transfer results. It is a function of `verdicts/` and of the code in this
repository, and of nothing else.

So this repository redistributes no third-party content. It publishes our own
measurements about benchmarks a reader obtains from their own publishers.


2. The constraint that shapes all of this
-----------------------------------------

Four of the eight datasets come from `lytang/LLM-AggreFact`, which is **CC BY-ND
4.0**, gated, and whose acceptance carries the condition that "Data in the
benchmark should not be used in pretraining or fine-tuning any NLP models".

Both clauses deserve a plain answer rather than silence.

  NoDerivatives.  We distribute no adapted or transformed copy of the benchmark.
  We distribute measurements about it. A reader must obtain the benchmark from its
  publisher, accepting the gate, exactly as we did.

  No pretraining or fine-tuning.  We do not train any language model on this data;
  it is used for evaluation only. The one supervised component in the method is a
  logistic regression over ten judges' binary verdicts, cross-fitted over held-out
  folds. It has ten features, never sees text, and is the object of study rather
  than a model being improved. We read the condition as aimed at benchmark
  contamination and believe this respects it, but state the fact so a reader can
  judge for themselves.

This is why the record schema carries no source text, and why it must not grow a
question, context or candidate field. That constraint is load-bearing, not
incidental.


